# --- registry -------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by setup/lib/models.sh; passed to llama-server as environment and
# ignored there. MODEL_SWA=yes means the profile MUST carry --swa-full —
# without it every Claude Code turn re-processes the whole prompt.
MODEL_TITLE=Judge/evals · 59.0 GiB · MXFP4 native · KV very cheap
MODEL_SWA=yes
# MODEL_SOURCE — where this model comes from, so the profile can fetch it.
# `<repo> <pattern>…`: every pattern is a substring of a path in that repo and
# every matching .gguf is fetched, so a sharded quant comes down whole and an
# mmproj rides along. Read by setup/get-model.sh, which is this stack's
# equivalent of `ollama pull` — except that the list it offers is MEASURED on
# this hardware (bash setup/lib/models.sh table) rather than a generic catalog.
# Verified 26.08. by matching the exact filename in the repo, not by guessing.
MODEL_SOURCE=ggml-org/gpt-oss-120b-GGUF gpt-oss-120b-MXFP4
# MODEL_KV_KIB_PER_TOKEN — measured. Read by setup/lib/budget.py.
MODEL_KV_KIB_PER_TOKEN=36.0
MODEL_KV_SOURCE=this profile's own note below: 4.5 GiB at -c 131072, i.e. 36.0 KiB per token.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Judge/evals · 59.0 GiB · MXFP4 native · KV very cheap (4.5 GiB @131k)
# Speculative decoding disabled: eagle3-gpt-oss-120b-Q8_0.gguf is missing (0.85 GB)
# -cram WAS 32768, copied from qwen38 where it was computed. Measured 27.08.
# (`budget.py --cache`) it buys 7.1 full windows here against qwen38's 2.2 —
# and this is the TIGHTEST profile in the registry:
#
#     weights 59.0 + KV 4.5 + buffers 6.4  =  69.9 GiB pinned in GTT
#     + RAM prompt cache 32.0 + host 12.0  = 113.9 of 124.9  -> 11 GiB spare
#     with -cram 16384 (3.6 windows)       =  97.9 of 124.9  -> 27 GiB spare
#
# qwen38's own note calls 32 GiB "provisioned about 4x above observed use,
# which is headroom rather than waste AT THIS FOOTPRINT". The qualifier is the
# point: at 59 GiB of weights the same number is not headroom.
# --- reasoning modes ------------------------------------------------------
#
# The rule and the vocabulary: setup/claude/modes.py. The two lines below are
# GENERATED — `python3 bench/suites/effort-vocabulary.py --profile gptoss` —
# and everything model-specific about them is the measurement that follows.
#
# The one profile whose levels are NOT measured here, and the reason matters.
# bench/suites/effort-vocabulary.py refuses to derive them, because this
# template validates nothing — it interpolates whatever it is given:
#
#     {{- "Reasoning: " + reasoning_effort + "\n\n" }}
#
# so `max` renders as happily as `low` and rendering proves nothing about what
# the MODEL was trained on. That is the quiet failure mode, worse than Qwen's
# loud one: an untrained word reaches the prompt and nothing reports it.
#
# The levels therefore come from the model card, with provenance: low / medium
# / high, "which trade off latency vs. performance", set as "Reasoning: <level>"
# in the system prompt — openai/gpt-oss-120b on Hugging Face and the gpt-oss
# model card (arXiv 2508.10925), read 28.08.2026. xhigh and max are not among
# them, so both are sent as high.
#
# No `none` mode: measured, this template ignores enable_thinking entirely (on,
# off and unset all render 189ebbae), so "do not think" is not expressible for
# this model at all. And no `medium`: it is the template's own default
# (line 204), so it would be a second cache key for the bare alias.
#
# TEMPLATE_LEVELS is empty because it cannot be measured, not because there is
# nothing to check — see above.
MODES=low:low  high:high  xhigh:high  max:high
TEMPLATE_LEVELS=unmeasurable
#
LLAMA_ARGS=--alias gptoss -m @MODELS@/gpt-oss-120b-MXFP4.gguf \
  -ngl 999 -fa on -ub 512 -b 2048 -c 131072 -ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0 \
  --kv-unified -cram 16384 \
  --jinja --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080

# Backend for this profile. Measured 24.08. (docs/MODELS.md): the choice
# is MODEL-dependent — Vulkan wins for models without speculation, ROCm wins
# 2x once MTP/ngram speculation is on. Inert until llama-user@.service is
# switched to: ExecStart=/bin/sh -c 'exec "$HOME/$LLAMA_BIN" $LLAMA_ARGS' (one sudo install).
LLAMA_BIN=llama.cpp/build-vulkan/bin/llama-server
